opencode installs npm packages into the user's home at runtime. reify() is
the single place any of it happens; the callers are

  - the plugin loader, which runs on every start, unprompted, and installs
    @opencode-ai/plugin into ~/.config/opencode/node_modules;
  - the formatter and LSP integrations, which fetch prettier, biome,
    typescript-language-server and friends on demand;
  - the provider loader, for model SDKs that are not already bundled.

A distribution package must not fetch and execute code from a third party
registry. The Npm interface declares InstallFailedError on every method, so
refusing here degrades rather than breaks, and a tool the user installed
themselves is still found on PATH.

OPENCODE_ALLOW_NPM_INSTALL=1 restores upstream behaviour.

